                          $-\\sqrt{9-(x-3)^2}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nConstruct an integral that represents the area of this circle using rectangular coordinates.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{0}^{6}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{9-(x-3)^2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\,\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nConstruct an integral that represents the arc length of this circle in rectangular coordinates.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{0}^{6}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        