      \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta $" 13194139535567 true] [17592186355450 1113 #uuid "ff226c50-e59e-5c6f-b42e-e5a324df1531" 13194139535567 true] [17592186355450 1145 "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{36({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}6\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535567 true] [17592186355451 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355452 13194139535567 true] [17592186355451 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535567 true] [17592186355451 1041 "field-1" 13194139535567 true] [17592186355451 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355452 13194139535567 true] [17592186355451 1110 #uuid "adbe6a1e-f97a-5a05-bd1a-08525fe36ed7" 13194139535567 true] [17592186355452 1034 "6" 13194139535567 true] [1759218635